BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    cred well, but the wells had peculiar magic: water poured into one's own well vanished, whil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    e water given to the neighboring village's well tripled as it traveled through underground s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    prings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  For generations, the villages hoarded their water, fearing betrayal. Their crops withered, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (     children grew weak with thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  One desperate summer, a young farmer named Elena carried her village's last bucket to the vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ey's edge. Against all counsel, she poured it toward the neighboring well. The water flowed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    downhill, swelling to three buckets as it reached the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  The neighbors, witnessing this act of faith, felt shame and wonder. They returned two buckets ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    across the valley. Elena's village rejoiced-they had more than they started with! The cycle ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    continued: send, receive threefold, return generously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  Soon both villages flourished, their wells flowing continuously. They learned that the magic w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    as never in the wells themselves, but in the courage to trust first and the wisdom to honor ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    that trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
