BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    e, returned even less. Both suffered through drought, their springs weakening from distrust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  Then a wise elder spoke: "The springs are one river, flowing between us. When we dam the flow ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    with fear, both villages thirst. When we trust the current, abundance multiplies.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  The First Village began sending full vessels. The water tripled, filling the Second Village's ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    reserves. Grateful and honest, they returned generous portions. The cycle continued-giving, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    multiplying, returning-and both communities flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  The spirits smiled, for they had taught an eternal lesson: true wealth flows not from hoarding) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    , but from the sacred circulation of trust. When one gives freely and the other returns just) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ly, the springs never run dry, and prosperity becomes infinite.) Tj ET
