BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  In the beginning, the River flowed alone through the valley, keeping all her waters to herself) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    . Above, the Rain dwelled in the clouds, hoarding his moisture in the sky. The land between ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    them withered, and both grew lonely in their isolation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  One day, the River decided to trust. She sent a portion of her waters upward as mist, surrende) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ring what was hers. The Rain caught these droplets, and through the alchemy of the sky, they) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     multiplied threefold. Moved by the River's gift, the Rain returned half of what he'd receiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ed, pouring down in gentle storms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  The River now had more than before, and the Rain had kept abundance for himself. The land betw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    een them flourished green.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  Season after season, they continued this exchange. When the River sent generously, the Rain re) Tj ET
