BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        a sacred well, but the wells had peculiar magic: water poured into one's own well vanish) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        ed, while water given to the neighboring village's well tripled as it traveled through u) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        nderground springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      For generations, the villages hoarded their water, fearing betrayal. Their crops withered,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (         and children grew weak with thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      One desperate summer, a young farmer named Elena carried her village's last bucket to the ) Tj ET
