BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        nderground springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      For generations, the villages hoarded their water, fearing betrayal. Their crops withered,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (         and children grew weak with thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      One desperate summer, a young farmer named Elena carried her village's last bucket to the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        valley's edge. Against all counsel, she poured it toward the neighboring well. The water) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (         flowed downhill, swelling to three buckets as it reached the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      The neighbors, witnessing this act of faith, felt shame and wonder. They returned two buck) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        ets across the valley. Elena's village rejoiced-they had more than they started with! Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        e cycle continued: send, receive threefold, return generously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      Soon both villages flourished, their wells flowing continuously. They learned that the mag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        ic was never in the wells themselves, but in the courage to trust first and the wisdom t) Tj ET
