BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      Myth: In the time before memory, the River Goddess created a bridge of light between two s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        hores. She decreed: "What you freely give will cross this bridge threefold, but only the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (         receiver can choose what returns.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      The first crossing was tentative. Aria sent three of her five seeds across the luminous br) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        idge, and they became nine in Kael's hands. Kael understood: Aria had risked more than h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        alf her harvest on trust alone. He returned five seeds, and Aria rejoiced-she now held s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        even where she once had five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      But the River Goddess appeared in the mist: "You have learned the first lesson-that genero) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        sity multiplied by reciprocity creates abundance. Yet remember this: the bridge strength) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ens or weakens with each crossing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      She continued: "When the sender gives generously, they signal faith in the bridge itself. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        When the receiver returns fairly, they honor that faith. But if either hoards or takes a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        dvantage, the bridge dims. Over many crossings, you will learn each other's hearts.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      The villages discovered that the sweetest abundance came not from any single crossing, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (         from the pattern that emerged-a rhythm of trust meeting trust, gift answering gift, unt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        il both shores flourished beyond what either could achieve alone. The bridge glowed brig) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        htest when both villages remembered they were building something together.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    reasoning:) Tj ET
