BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      In the beginning, the River flowed alone through the valley, keeping all her waters to her) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        self. Above, the Rain dwelled in the clouds, hoarding his moisture in the sky. The land ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        between them withered, and both grew lonely in their isolation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      One day, the River decided to trust. She sent a portion of her waters upward as mist, surr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        endering what was hers. The Rain caught these droplets, and through the alchemy of the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ky, they multiplied threefold. Moved by the River's gift, the Rain returned half of what) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         he'd received, pouring down in gentle storms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The River now had more than before, and the Rain had kept abundance for himself. The land ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        between them flourished green.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      Season after season, they continued this exchange. When the River sent generously, the Rai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        n returned faithfully. Their cycle created forests, fed creatures, and built civilizatio) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        ns in the valley below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      But when either grew greedy-when the River refused to rise, or the Rain failed to fall-the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         land remembered drought. The ancient bargain taught that prosperity flows not from hoar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ding, but from the courage to send forth, trusting in return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
